WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Finding the full text. Then checking it is the right paper.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.458
Filling one field. Then searching the source again.

00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:16.208
Different answers from colleagues. Now, reconstructing why.

00:00:16.208 --> 00:00:22.083
I brought these steps into one workbench. Here is a real example.

00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:26.500
Click the PDF page number to go back to the source.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.875
The highlight helps you find it. Read the context before accepting the code.

00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:38.042
Need a change? Choose Revise and explain why.

00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:42.458
Checked and supported? Choose Correct.

00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:47.167
One skill retrieves full texts and checks their identity.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:52.875
The other prepares review packages from your rules and organizes team returns.

00:00:52.875 --> 00:01:01.292
People develop rules, verify evidence, and resolve disagreements. Next, see how the two skills work.
